        <briefdescription>
<para>Strain increment from nodal displacement increments, without forming the B-operator. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The symmetric part of the incremental displacement gradient <formula id="32">$\partial_\mathbf{x} \Delta\mathbf{u} = \Delta\mathbf{U}\, \partial_\mathbf{x}\mathbf{N}^\mathsf{T}$</formula>, with the nodal increments <formula id="33">$\Delta\mathbf{U}$</formula> arranged as a nDim x nNodes matrix, in Voigt notation with engineering shear strains. This is <formula id="34">$\mathbf{B}\, \Delta\mathbf{\qu}$</formula> with a sixth (3D) of the data and half of the operations of the dense product. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nDim</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of spatial dimensions (1, 2 or 3). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nNodes</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of element nodes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">dQU</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Incremental nodal displacements, node-wise (u1, u2, u3 of node 1, then node 2, ...). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">dNdX</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Shape function gradients with respect to the physical coordinates (nDim x nNodes). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The strain increment in (plane) Voigt notation. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
